    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Telord72612/Bathing-in-Skyrim-SN-SA-Plugins/tarball/V2.6.0",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Telord72612/Bathing-in-Skyrim-SN-SA-Plugins/zipball/V2.6.0",
    "body": "**For SkyrimNet 0.25.0 (Beta 25) and newer.** For Beta 24 or older, the last build is [V2.4.1](../../releases/tag/V2.4.1); that line is no longer updated.\r\n\r\n### What changed\r\n\r\n- **Walking to water indoors now works.** The bundled Standpoint is updated from 0.7.0 to 1.0.0. The old version checked for hostile NPCs in a way that, inside any building, also counted NPCs from other, unloaded buildings. A follower sent to a bath-house pool had her walk cancelled half a second after it started, and was told something dangerous was in the way. Outdoor walks were not affected.\r\n- **No more rescue by teleport.** A follower who got stuck on her way to the water could be thrown forward by the old stuck recovery, sometimes through a wall or the floor. She now gives up and says she could not reach the water.\r\n- **The SkyrimNet plugin id changed** to match the SkyrimNet Hub listing. It is now `telord72612.bathing-in-skyrim-renewed-integration-for-skyrimnet` (it was `telord.bisr-sn-sa`).\r\n\r\nNothing else changed: same actions, same prompt, same Papyrus bridge, same FOMOD options, SE / AE / VR.\r\n\r\n### Updating from V2.5.0\r\n\r\n**Replace the old version, do not merge.** If your mod manager merged the two, delete the folder `SKSE/Plugins/SkyrimNet/external/telord.bisr-sn-sa/`. Safe on existing saves.\r\n\r\nIf you also run the standalone [Standpoint](https://github.com/Telord72612/Standpoint) mod, let whichever copy is newer win.\r\n\r\n### Requirements\r\n\r\nUnchanged: SkyrimNet 0.25.0+, Bathing in Skyrim - Renewed 2.79+, SeverActions (survival enabled), PapyrusUtil, po3's Papyrus Extender, SKSE + Address Library, and on VR the `skyrimvresl` loader. Water Finder and Standpoint 1.0.0 are bundled. Wash Me - Renewed stays optional for the paired washing actions.\r\n"
  },
